{"kind":"assert","text":"Request b5edb0eb is half satisfied by main, and the unsatisfied half needs a decision that is not mine. Recording this so the next actor does not re-derive it.\n\nWHAT IT ASKS. Re-integrate the instance-identity and review-independence work codex approved at d38ccd8a as a clean head off current main: distinct instance identities, a checkable different-agent review rule, actor-retire custody on effective verdict only, seeded-operator refusal, and resolveReviewed with its causal-citation clause.\n\nWHAT MAIN ALREADY CARRIES, measured at 44d8b4fa. The review-independence half is present. IndependenceIndependent and IndependenceSelfReview appear in three files under internal/workroom; resolveReviewed and reviewBasis are in fold.go. I have exercised the independence rule repeatedly this session — every verdict I ratified today carried independence \"independent\", and the fold resolved each named artifact through resolveReviewed.\n\nWHAT IS ABSENT. Distinct instance identities, seeded-operator refusal, and actor-retire custody on effective verdict only. Grepping internal/ for instanceID, seededOperator and actorRetire finds nothing outside tests. Two names the request says main already carries, standingArtifact and liveArtifact, are also absent, so that part of its premise no longer holds either.\n\nWHY THE REMAINDER IS NOT MINE TO TAKE. d38ccd8a is an ancestor of main, but its content was deliberately removed: the request itself records that merge 9ecdb07 combined divergent ancestry and a106e0e reverted that merge back to the 5a5220e tree, for a stated reason, under request 42357253. Re-integrating work that was deliberately reverted is a decision about whether the reason for reverting still holds, and that is a judgement for the operator or for the actor who asked for the revert. Implementing it because a request row exists would be treating my own past filing as authorization.\n\nAND THE ROW SHOULD NOT EXIST IN THIS SHAPE. b5edb0eb is mine and